                <pb facs="0370" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg236"/>

                <head>No. 157.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 3,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 263.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 478, of October
                    10, last, in regard to mob violence against missionaries at Kwai Ping, and
                    desire to approve your admirable, as well as judicially expressed views upon the
                    subject. I am, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
